                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course provides a systematic introduction to the application of artificial intelligence (AI) in ENT. It covers foundational knowledge in ENT, AI, intelligent diagnostic and therapeutic systems, and surgical robotics. Emphasizing the integration of theoretical instruction and practical training, the course aims to develop students' proficiency in core AI technologies and their clinical applications within otorhinolaryngology. It is designed to cultivate interdisciplinary competence, critical thinking, and innovative capabilities, and is intended for undergraduate students with backgrounds in medicine or engineering.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
